<title>USA: Telular says court upholds core patents.</title>
<headline>Telular says court upholds core patents.</headline>
<dateline>BUFFALO GROVE, Ill. 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telular Corp said Wednesday it received the opinion of the U.S. Court of Appeals upholding the company's core patents.</p>
<p>Telular said it received the opinion of the United States Court of Appeals for the Federal Circuit in the case of Arthur L. Serrano and Andrew W. Holman v. Telular Corporation, 96-1308.</p>
<p>The court unanimously affirmed the lower court's decision, concluding that U.S. Patents 4,775,997 and 4,922,517, owned by Telular, were valid and infringed, the company said.</p>
<p>The Telular intellectual property consists of a system for interfacing a standard telephone with a radio transceiver.</p>
<p>Telular develops telecommunications interface technology.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
